**2. Register in `Program.cs`:**

```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// Add Problem Details services
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<GlobalExceptionHandler>();

var app = builder.Build();

// Must be before route mapping
app.UseExceptionHandler();

app.MapGet("/example", () => { throw new KeyNotFoundException("Item not found"); });

app.Run();
```

**How it works:**

- `IExceptionHandler` (added in .NET 8) integrates with the built-in exception handler middleware — no per-endpoint try-catch needed.
- `AddProblemDetails()` configures the response format as RFC 7807 (`application/problem+json`).
- For 500s, the exception message is suppressed to avoid leaking internals.
- You can chain multiple `IExceptionHandler` implementations (they run in registration order; return `false` to pass to the next).

**Example 404 response:**
```json
{
  "type": "https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc9110#section-15.5.5",
  "title": "Not Found",
  "status": 404,
  "detail": "Item not found"
}
```
